node_modules/
dist/
.next/
next-env.d.ts
*.log
.DS_Store
.mtg-tutor/
scratch/
.omc/
.turbo/
# Every env file holds keys except the committed examples, so the rule is
# suffix-blind: `.env.local.cloud-dev`, kept while switching between a cloud and
# a local deployment, is exactly as secret as the `.env.local` it copies.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.tsbuildinfo

# A local Convex deployment's SQLite database, written by `convex dev` when the
# selected deployment is `local:`. Rebuildable from the seed pipeline.
.convex/

# 17Lands datasets and what the scripts reduce them to. Build inputs only --
# ~1.2GB per set raw, reduced to a ~270KB artifact under packages/backend/data,
# which IS committed. Everything here is re-derivable from a public URL, so it
# is cached rather than stored: the card snapshots `cache-cards` writes, and the
# dealt packs `fit-bot-policy` and `bench-bots` read (~20MB a set, and the
# difference between a fifteen-minute run and a four-second one). Both carry a
# fingerprint of what they were derived from and rebuild themselves when it
# moves, which is why a stale cache here cannot quietly change a number.
datasets/

# What `refresh-mechanics` downloads: the Comprehensive Rules, and Scryfall's
# card text per set. The Scryfall half is an ordinary cache, the same contract as
# datasets/ above.
#
# The rules are NOT. They must never be committed, whatever the size: the Fan
# Content Policy permits a great deal and carves verbatim republication of
# Wizards' rules content out of it, so a copy of that file in this repo is the
# one thing here that would actually be a breach. It is a dev-time input that
# decides which mechanics exist and supplies a section number to cite; every
# sentence a person reads is written by us in packages/core/docs/set-mechanics.yaml,
# and `checkOriginal` fails the run if one of them drifts back into the original.
packages/backend/.cache/

# The upstream 17Lands CSVs, kept by `pnpm archive-datasets` and read by nothing
# automatically. The opposite contract to `datasets/` above, which is why it is a
# separate directory rather than a subfolder: those files are caches that rebuild
# themselves from a fingerprint, and these are kept precisely BECAUSE they may
# stop being fetchable. ~700MB for the sets we ship, and re-downloadable only for
# as long as 17Lands serves them -- so it is ignored for size, not because losing
# it would be cheap.
archive/

# Benchmark output, and only the derived half. `pnpm bench-report` rebuilds the
# page from a transcript in milliseconds for free, so it is build output.
#
# The transcripts under bench/ are NOT ignored, and the distinction is not
# "how often does it change". A seed pins the deal and the prompts byte-for-byte
# but not the model's generation, so a run costs ~350k tokens and its prose can
# never be reproduced -- least of all the runs whose cut got REJECTED, which
# never become a baseline and would otherwise leave no record of why.
packages/backend/bench/report.*.html

# Scratch checkouts the agent harness makes to work on several branches at once.
# They are real worktrees of this repo, so they carry a full tree each and would
# otherwise be offered for commit from whichever one is being worked in.
.claude/worktrees
